# P3. Every graph is a known graph; every runtime graph belongs to a declared
# DHB (B4; D1 condition 3, check 3, Pass B form).
# Lists every graph holding triples that is not one of the three kg graphs,
# the shapes graph, or a declared DHB's dbr or dsr graph: a runtime graph
# whose dhbId is not declared, a malformed runtime graph name, a misspelt kg
# graph, a graph outside the scheme, and the stored default graph if anything
# is in it. Since P2 keeps runtime instances (records included) in runtime
# graphs, P2 and P3 together say: every platform record sits in a graph of a
# declared DHB.
# Rows = breaches. No rows = every graph is one the scheme names.
# {{KNOWN_GRAPHS}} = from the templates module and the declared DHBs:
#   <https://ontara.dev/graph/kg/metamodel>, <https://ontara.dev/graph/kg/domain>,
#   <https://ontara.dev/graph/kg/correspondence>, <https://ontara.dev/graph/shapes>,
#   and for each declared (tenant, dhbId): <.../dhb/{tenant}/{dhbId}/dbr>, <.../dhb/{tenant}/{dhbId}/dsr>
# Pass B: the declared DHBs are the stack configuration's (the Cafe's RRB only).
# Pass C: read from the RIR's declarations in the RRB's dsr graph instead.
SELECT ?g (COUNT(*) AS ?triples)
WHERE {
  {
    GRAPH ?g { ?s ?p ?o }
    FILTER (?g NOT IN ( {{KNOWN_GRAPHS}} ))
  }
  UNION
  {
    GRAPH <{{STORED_DEFAULT_GRAPH}}> { ?s ?p ?o }
    BIND (<{{STORED_DEFAULT_GRAPH}}> AS ?g)
  }
}
GROUP BY ?g
ORDER BY ?g
